jeff@dirac.physics.sunysb.edu (Jeff Althoff) writes:
>    On another debug-mode level, anyone know why it's so hard to hit 
>    something with a +100 Stormbringer? Wind up missing a lot, but when you
>    do hit, instant oblivion...

Overflow.  Your to-hit roll is a signed character, -128 to 127.

When that +100 is added to the broadsword's to-hit value, the
monster's AC, and your level and luck values, it's likely to exceed
127 and wrap around to a very negative number.

Normally, it's rare to get a weapon into the +10 range without it
evaporating.  Only a wizard could wish up a +100 weapon.  


